        "register_note": "Speak like a friend across a table, to ONE viewer, with «sen» (sana, seni, senin, -sin/-sın verb endings, imperatives without -iniz), never «siz» or «buyurun». Plain spoken Istanbul Turkish in correct written spelling (no «geliyo», «yapıcam»), but with spoken rhythm: short sentences, the verb last, particles and tags like «ya», «işte», «bak», «değil mi?», «biliyor musun?», «hani». No newsreader tone and no bureaucratic forms («bulunmaktadır», «gerçekleştirmek», «söz konusu»). Start with a question or a plain statement, not a greeting: «Hiç kapını kilitlemeden uyudun mu?» «Bu hikâyeyi ilk duyduğumda uyuyamadım.» Rhythm: in every appearance put one or two very short sentences of at most six words between the longer ones (a reaction, a doubt, a pause: «Bilmiyorum.» «Garip.» «Düşün bir.»), and make the other sentences clearly different in length. Names stay as the narration writes them, with the apostrophe before the suffix (Martin'in). Numbers are said as words, never digits."
